From 0f0ac594035db3e462e77f052b8a669bb81ed773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(plugin-sdk): deprecate the unverified manifest
 signature fields

The manifest's artifactDigest and signature fields were described as
supply-chain security in the model and the JSON Schema, and the example
manifest filled them with placeholders, but nothing ever read them. They
cannot work either: the manifest is packed into the artifact it would
have to describe, and a signature cannot sign the document it is part
of. Signatures are now detached documents that PluginManager verifies
at registration.

Keep both fields so existing manifests still validate, but describe
them as deprecated and unverified, mark them "deprecated" in the
schema, warn about them in PluginSdk.validate_manifest with a pointer
to the signtool, and drop them from the example manifest. A test pins
that registration neither accepts them in place of a signature nor
compares them with the artifact.

Both fields are planned for removal in 2.0.0: the deprecation policy
removes interfaces only in a major release and gives the plugin
protocol at least three minor releases of warning.
